        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): drop blank entries from trailing commas in agenda/device directives",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe LINE `[[agenda:]]` and `[[device:]]` directive parsers split their comma-separated lists without dropping blank entries. A trailing or doubled comma in agent output (common in LLM text) produces empty model entries:\n\n- **agenda** → an empty-title event → an empty-string Flex `text` component. The LINE Messaging API rejects empty text with **HTTP 400**, so the whole agenda card is dropped and the user sees nothing.\n- **device** → a control whose `label` is empty, which is likewise invalid.\n\nThe `[[quick_replies:]]` parser already avoids this by routing its split through the shared `normalizeStringEntries` helper (which trims and drops empties). Agenda and device did not, so a stray comma silently loses the message.\n\nFixes #105380\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth parsers now route their comma-lists through the same `normalizeStringEntries` helper that `[[quick_replies:]]` uses, instead of an ad-hoc split. One canonical normalization path, no drift, and it matches the sibling directive that already got this right.\n\nScope note: `[[buttons:]]` is intentionally left out. Its blank-entry case is already handled on `main` by the `.filter((action) => action.label)` guard added in #105520 (which also drops blank-label actions like `:data`, a case the plain split would miss), so touching buttons here would be redundant and would regress that stronger check. This PR is scoped to the two directives that are still affected.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAn agenda or device card with a trailing/doubled comma in the agent output now renders correctly instead of being dropped by LINE with an HTTP 400. No behavior change for well-formed input.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 1. Real LINE API — the actual directive-generated payload\n\n`parseLineDirectives(\"[[agenda: Today | Standup:9am, Lunch:12pm,]]\")` output posted to the LINE `validate/push` endpoint (validates a payload without sending; token/recipient redacted):\n\n**Before (current `main`):**\n```\naltText: 📋 Today (3 events)\nHTTP 400 - {\"message\":\"A message (messages[0]) in the request body is invalid\",\n  \"details\":[{\"message\":\"must be non-empty text\",\n  \"property\":\"/body/contents/2/contents/2/contents/2/contents/0/text\"}]}\n```\n\n**After (this PR):**\n```\naltText: 📋 Today (2 events)\nHTTP 200 - {}\n```\n\nThe 400 points at the empty `text` component deep inside the real agenda card; after the fix the generated payload validates.\n\n### 2. Source-level reproduction (`parseLineDirectives`, current `main`)\n\n| directive (trailing/doubled comma) | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[[agenda: Today \\| Standup:9am, Lunch:12pm,]]` | 3 events, 1 empty `text` component | 2 events, 0 |\n| `[[device: TV \\| Box \\| Playing \\| Play:toggle,, Menu:menu]]` | 1 empty control label | 0 |\n\n### 3. Tests\n\nNew regression tests in `reply-payload-transform.test.ts` (trailing-comma agenda, doubled-comma device). Verified red on `main`, green with the fix:\n\n```\n# without the fix (revert the two normalizeStringEntries calls):\n × drops trailing commas in agenda events\n × drops doubled commas in device controls\n Tests  2 failed | 18 passed (20)\n\n# with the fix:\n Tests  20 passed (20)\n```\n\n`oxfmt --check`, `oxlint`, and the extension typecheck are clean on the touched files.\n",
        "branch": "fix/line-directive-empty-entries",
